(159435, 8678, 4514, '<td valign="top">Nice idea.  Needed more natural light to sell this photo.  Hmmmm.  Wondering how I would have set this up.  will get back to you.</td>', 'Nice idea.  Needed more natural light to sell this photo.  Hmmmm.  Wondering how I would have set this up.  will get back to you.', '2002-11-26 03:53:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(159436, 8678, 4162, '<td valign="top">The flash on the foreground is a little strong but the picture is interesting.</td>', 'The flash on the foreground is a little strong but the picture is interesting.', '2002-11-26 20:45:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(159437, 8678, 2337, '<td valign="top">The light seems a bit harsh.  Not sure if you could have controlled it, but it looks like you used flash... The rock and plants at the bottom are overexposed.  Nice composition!  My eye is drawn to the fog/mouth... ~ Myqyl ~</td>', 'The light seems a bit harsh.  Not sure if you could have controlled it, but it looks like you used flash... The rock and plants at the bottom are overexposed.  Nice composition!  My eye is drawn to the fog/mouth... ~ Myqyl ~', '2002-11-26 21:20:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(159438, 8678, 640, '<td valign="top">Interesting! Is this hot steam? Would have prefered sharper focus.</td>', 'Interesting! Is this hot steam? Would have prefered sharper focus.', '2002-11-27 00:53:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(159439, 8678, 2490, '<td valign="top">Hmmm.  I can''t decide if I like the green or not, but the foreground being flashed/washed out does bother me.  A little toning down on the brightness and pumping up the contrast would probably have been good.  7 nards656<br/></td>', 'Hmmm.  I can''t decide if I like the green or not, but the foreground being flashed/washed out does bother me.  A little toning down on the brightness and pumping up the contrast would probably have been good.  7 nards656', '2002-11-27 21:21:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(159440, 8678, 3018, '<td valign="top">Nice picture, try to avoid using the flash.  I don''t think mayans used that kind of figures, but maybe I''m wrong.</td>', 'Nice picture, try to avoid using the flash.  I don''t think mayans used that kind of figures, but maybe I''m wrong.', '2002-11-28 11:33:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(159441, 8678, 4648, '<td valign="top">A little tight on the crop at the top.  Will the article tell what''s coming out the mouth and what the things are inside it.  Zoomed out would be a 10.  But still good shot.  PTL8</td>', 'A little tight on the crop at the top.  Will the article tell what''s coming out the mouth and what the things are inside it.  Zoomed out would be a 10.  But still good shot.  PTL8', '2002-11-28 20:34:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(159442, 8678, 3540, '<td valign="top">The flash in this pic makes the vegetation in the foreground look very fake.  The subject in this pic is awesome though.  I might have tried to frame the shot so that the foreground vegetation was minimal and the top of the figures head was included.  That probably would''ve helped your score by 2 points.  Still an interesting shot.  - Inspzil</td>', 'The flash in this pic makes the vegetation in the foreground look very fake.  The subject in this pic is awesome though.  I might have tried to frame the shot so that the foreground vegetation was minimal and the top of the figures head was included.  That probably would''ve helped your score by 2 points.  Still an interesting shot.  - Inspzil', '2002-11-29 05:03:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(159443, 8678, 244, '<td valign="top">Nice picture, no news.  Dosen''t tell a story. 4 -Corey</td>', 'Nice picture, no news.  Dosen''t tell a story. 4 -Corey', '2002-11-29 21:17:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(159444, 8678, 3279, '<td valign="top">I''ve no idea what I''m looking at, and your flash is too strong on the foreground - but I do like that effect on the water...</td>', 'I''ve no idea what I''m looking at, and your flash is too strong on the foreground - but I do like that effect on the water...', '2002-11-30 13:55:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(159445, 8678, 4411, '<td valign="top">The flash has made the lighting &amp; shadows very harsh on this. I''m not a big fan of flash shots - a tripod &amp; long exposure would make a better shot IMO. Composition is nice though, and I like the subject.</td>', 'The flash has made the lighting & shadows very harsh on this. I''m not a big fan of flash shots - a tripod & long exposure would make a better shot IMO. Composition is nice though, and I like the subject.', '2002-11-30 20:36:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(159446, 8678, 5070, '<td valign="top">This would be more effective with rock cropped out of foreground.</td>', 'This would be more effective with rock cropped out of foreground.', '2002-11-30 20:46:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(159447, 8678, 2221, '<td valign="top">I like the effect that the water looks so soft because of the motion blur. But the lighting looks bad. I guess you used a flash. This makes the photo look very unnatural and this does not fit to your subject. Now it looks like a photo made of a setup in a photo studio.  -stephan</td>', 'I like the effect that the water looks so soft because of the motion blur. But the lighting looks bad. I guess you used a flash. This makes the photo look very unnatural and this does not fit to your subject. Now it looks like a photo made of a setup in a photo studio.  -stephan', '2002-12-01 09:59:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(159448, 8678, 2, '<td valign="top">Your flash is really harsh in the front.  Most of the image is very loud, and it''s difficult to find a focal point.</td>', 'Your flash is really harsh in the front.  Most of the image is very loud, and it''s difficult to find a focal point.', '2002-12-01 23:15:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(159449, 8678, 4927, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments everyone, they were very helpful. I''m kind of new to digital photography and this was my first challenge. Hopefully, I''ll be able to learn a few things here and improve my photo taking ability. I look forward to any more advice/suggestions that anyone can offer, just email me.<br/><br/>I realize that the lighting was harsh because of the flash. I don''t have a tripod yet (hopefully for christmas), so I had to use the flash much to my dismay (I probably should have cropped the photo better).</td>', 'Thanks for the comments everyone, they were very helpful. I''m kind of new to digital photography and this was my first challenge. Hopefully, I''ll be able to learn a few things here and improve my photo taking ability. I look forward to any more advice/suggestions that anyone can offer, just email me.I realize that the lighting was harsh because of the flash. I don''t have a tripod yet (hopefully for christmas), so I had to use the flash much to my dismay (I probably should have cropped the photo better).', '2002-12-02 00:24:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(159450, 8678, 4493, '<td valign="top">~~~~Critique Club Comment~~~~<br/>Mayan Mysteries<br/><br/>*Composition (content)*<br/>This picture appears to have been taken standing right in front of the subject matter. To help give some interest to the composition, you may have wanted to try kneeling down to give a lower perspective. The lower vantage point may have uncovered more of the eye on the right of the frame, as well as fill the <br/><br/>whole frame with the face so as to not have the white area to the left of the head. The green branches in the foreground are a nice contrast to the stone in the back.<br/><br/>*Background*<br/>The white area to the left of the head as well as the reflection of the flash in the mouth are somewhat distracting to the eye. If there was a way you could either take the shot with a longer exposure and no flash, or to bounce your flash off something else the washout of the plants in the foreground would be less, as well as artifacts in the background.<br/><br/><br/>*Camera Work (Technical)*<br/>Too much flash in the foreground. Your focus and depth of field are good. You have great detail in the leaves and stone work.<br/><br/>*Digital Processing (technical)*<br/>Sharpening is very good (not too soft and no trace of over sharpening).<br/>Balance between light and dark is fair. Would like to see the brightness of the flash toned down.<br/>Compression is good (no jpeg artifacts)<br/><br/>*My opinion*<br/>I think this is an interesting subject. The fog out of the mouth adds character. I do however think that if you were to change the perspective of the camera and have a way to lessen the washout of the flash, you could create a sense of stumbling upon an ancient ruin somewhere in Mexico.<br/></td>', '~~~~Critique Club Comment~~~~Mayan Mysteries*Composition (content)*This picture appears to have been taken standing right in front of the subject matter. To help give some interest to the composition, you may have wanted to try kneeling down to give a lower perspective. The lower vantage point may have uncovered more of the eye on the right of the frame, as well as fill the whole frame with the face so as to not have the white area to the left of the head. The green branches in the foreground are a nice contrast to the stone in the back.*Background*The white area to the left of the head as well as the reflection of the flash in the mouth are somewhat distracting to the eye. If there was a way you could either take the shot with a longer exposure and no flash, or to bounce your flash off something else the washout of the plants in the foreground would be less, as well as artifacts in the background.*Camera Work (Technical)*Too much flash in the foreground. Your focus and depth of field are good. You have great detail in the leaves and stone work.*Digital Processing (technical)*Sharpening is very good (not too soft and no trace of over sharpening).Balance between light and dark is fair. Would like to see the brightness of the flash toned down.Compression is good (no jpeg artifacts)*My opinion*I think this is an interesting subject. The fog out of the mouth adds character. I do however think that if you were to change the perspective of the camera and have a way to lessen the washout of the flash, you could create a sense of stumbling upon an ancient ruin somewhere in Mexico.', '2002-12-02 14:40:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(159451, 8680, 4967, '<td valign="top">Nice picture, very beautiful, but doesn''t really fit the challenge.</td>', 'Nice picture, very beautiful, but doesn''t really fit the challenge.', '2002-11-25 00:55:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(159452, 8680, 3032, '<td valign="top">Too much jpeg artifacts around the edges of the objects, save it at a higher quality. This pic is 42kb where 150 is allowed. The artifacts are very disturbing and it ruins the fluent transition of colors.<br/>I wonder what it would look like if it was shot from a position somewhat more to the left.</td>', 'Too much jpeg artifacts around the edges of the objects, save it at a higher quality. This pic is 42kb where 150 is allowed. The artifacts are very disturbing and it ruins the fluent transition of colors.I wonder what it would look like if it was shot from a position somewhat more to the left.', '2002-11-25 05:15:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(159453, 8680, 4482, '<td valign="top">Nice pic.. but what does it have to do with the theme??</td>', 'Nice pic.. but what does it have to do with the theme??', '2002-11-25 10:49:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(159454, 8680, 5379, '<td valign="top">great picture, what has it do with photojournalism?</td>', 'great picture, what has it do with photojournalism?', '2002-11-25 18:29:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(159455, 8680, 3447, '<td valign="top">This is a terrific photograph and should place very high in the voting.  Whether it fits my definition of journalism is an open question.  As a magazine photo it is very good indeed.  Front page of a newspaper - no.<br/>                                               6                  JEM</td>', 'This is a terrific photograph and should place very high in the voting.  Whether it fits my definition of journalism is an open question.  As a magazine photo it is very good indeed.  Front page of a newspaper - no.                                               6                  JEM', '2002-11-25 22:26:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(159456, 8680, 4267, '<td valign="top">I really like how the sun is seen through the arch... a great angle... I suppose it does meets the challenge in some way... but there''s no "impact of the moment" for me... (7)<br/>~anachronite</td>', 'I really like how the sun is seen through the arch... a great angle... I suppose it does meets the challenge in some way... but there''s no "impact of the moment" for me... (7)~anachronite', '2002-11-25 22:45:00.000000', NULL, 1),
