(159811, 8710, 806, '<td valign="top">Excellent catch! Could be a bit clearer, but nice all the same.</td>', 'Excellent catch! Could be a bit clearer, but nice all the same.', '2002-12-01 22:46:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(159812, 8710, 4967, '<td valign="top">To those who took the time to comment on my photo, thanks so much!  The comments were really appreciated, and I was joyful everytime I came back to the site and there was another comment!  I''m really excited I did this well, as this was my first entry for this site, and also this was the second hockey game I ever shot!   I was lucky to have a press pass to be able to shoot this for my school (Cornell University) yearbook!  Thanks again to everyone!</td>', 'To those who took the time to comment on my photo, thanks so much!  The comments were really appreciated, and I was joyful everytime I came back to the site and there was another comment!  I''m really excited I did this well, as this was my first entry for this site, and also this was the second hockey game I ever shot!   I was lucky to have a press pass to be able to shoot this for my school (Cornell University) yearbook!  Thanks again to everyone!', '2002-12-02 01:35:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(159813, 8710, 1019, '<td valign="top">Andrew<br/><br/>Critique Club<br/><br/>A wonderful photo. Sports photos are murder to get because you need the snap focus and speed and anticipation to capture the momentand that is what sports is all aboutthe moment. <br/><br/>The composition of the shot is excellentthe circle of tension between the two players facing off and the object of the game suspended in the middle until it gets hitwhat a moment! All the attention of the players is concentrated on that tiny object and it shows.<br/><br/>The exposure is greatit is so easy to underexpose the players because of the bright white ice. But the details are there even in the dark parts of the uniform.The focus is crisp with only the movement of the sticks blurringthis adds to the motion of the shot<br/><br/>I like the way you only see the side view of the faces covered in their masksvery powerful.<br/><br/>Your processing looks correct and no sign of digital nasties. All in all a great action shotwell done!<br/><br/></td>', 'AndrewCritique ClubA wonderful photo. Sports photos are murder to get because you need the snap focus and speed and anticipation to capture the momentand that is what sports is all aboutthe moment. The composition of the shot is excellentthe circle of tension between the two players facing off and the object of the game suspended in the middle until it gets hitwhat a moment! All the attention of the players is concentrated on that tiny object and it shows.The exposure is greatit is so easy to underexpose the players because of the bright white ice. But the details are there even in the dark parts of the uniform.The focus is crisp with only the movement of the sticks blurringthis adds to the motion of the shotI like the way you only see the side view of the faces covered in their masksvery powerful.Your processing looks correct and no sign of digital nasties. All in all a great action shotwell done!', '2002-12-02 13:36:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(159814, 8710, 4967, '<td valign="top">It would be interesting to see the reasonings for the people who gave me and other people 1''s.  I wish that those who did would leave a comment on why, if your going to give it... OWN UP TO IT!  Thanks Andrew for the critique, I really appreciate it!</td>', 'It would be interesting to see the reasonings for the people who gave me and other people 1''s.  I wish that those who did would leave a comment on why, if your going to give it... OWN UP TO IT!  Thanks Andrew for the critique, I really appreciate it!', '2002-12-02 21:53:00.000000', NULL, 0),
