(160024, 8723, 4648, '<td valign="top">Beautiful sunset.  Rule of thirds does not work to your advantage here in my opinion.  Your subject is the sunset but you hve more of the sky than the sunset.  Should have cropped of most of the sky.   The tree and the sunset are beautiful and should have encompased the photo.  This is what I call good composition but bad execution.  Otherwise nice shot.  PTL7</td>', 'Beautiful sunset.  Rule of thirds does not work to your advantage here in my opinion.  Your subject is the sunset but you hve more of the sky than the sunset.  Should have cropped of most of the sky.   The tree and the sunset are beautiful and should have encompased the photo.  This is what I call good composition but bad execution.  Otherwise nice shot.  PTL7', '2002-12-01 14:22:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(160025, 8723, 3050, '<td valign="top">Don''t see any connection to the theme, but man what a sunset.</td>', 'Don''t see any connection to the theme, but man what a sunset.', '2002-12-01 23:16:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(160026, 8723, 772, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club :)<br/><br/>Doug, I think this is definitely a beautiful sunset photo.  I definitely like the placement of your horizon low in the frame... the sky is the subject here and seeing more of that is important.  As I look at the image, I think the tree could be a little sharper silhouette.  F3.4 is possibly a little larger aperture than necessary for this shot.  I would have started this one at F5.6 in aperture priority mode and bracketed with extra exposures one stop up and down from there.  I believe that a smaller aperture would have sharpened up the tree against the background quite a bit.  Metering for a photograph like this is very difficult.... The key is to take a lot of photos at different settings and do it in a hurry.  Sunsets like these are constantly changing and they don''t last long.  <br/><br/>As for this photo and the photojournalism challenge, I''m not sure.  I haven''t read all the comments you received, but IMO, this is photojournalism, but not as much for news as it is for weather.  The term ''photojournalism'' usually strikes a sense of ''news'' and ''action'' in my mind.  I have browsed many books of ''photojournalism'' such as the Time/Life photo books and National Geographic as well.  Your photo fits better into the national geographic schema than into time/life stuff.  <br/><br/>John Setzler</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club :)Doug, I think this is definitely a beautiful sunset photo.  I definitely like the placement of your horizon low in the frame... the sky is the subject here and seeing more of that is important.  As I look at the image, I think the tree could be a little sharper silhouette.  F3.4 is possibly a little larger aperture than necessary for this shot.  I would have started this one at F5.6 in aperture priority mode and bracketed with extra exposures one stop up and down from there.  I believe that a smaller aperture would have sharpened up the tree against the background quite a bit.  Metering for a photograph like this is very difficult.... The key is to take a lot of photos at different settings and do it in a hurry.  Sunsets like these are constantly changing and they don''t last long.  As for this photo and the photojournalism challenge, I''m not sure.  I haven''t read all the comments you received, but IMO, this is photojournalism, but not as much for news as it is for weather.  The term ''photojournalism'' usually strikes a sense of ''news'' and ''action'' in my mind.  I have browsed many books of ''photojournalism'' such as the Time/Life photo books and National Geographic as well.  Your photo fits better into the national geographic schema than into time/life stuff.  John Setzler', '2002-12-02 13:24:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(160027, 8724, 221, '<td valign="top">Good content, exposure is about 1 stop over exposed and try not to cut a sign in two with a tree</td>', 'Good content, exposure is about 1 stop over exposed and try not to cut a sign in two with a tree', '2002-11-25 02:12:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(160028, 8724, 3127, '<td valign="top">I know balancing the components of this photo may have been difficult. Have the sign partially blocked by the tree takes a little away from the overall feel.</td>', 'I know balancing the components of this photo may have been difficult. Have the sign partially blocked by the tree takes a little away from the overall feel.', '2002-11-25 11:05:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(160029, 8724, 4411, '<td valign="top">I don''t think the tree has helped here, obscuring the sign and placcard. Maybe there was a better shot a few steps to your right? Could have done with a few more protesters too, but that''s not really under you control!</td>', 'I don''t think the tree has helped here, obscuring the sign and placcard. Maybe there was a better shot a few steps to your right? Could have done with a few more protesters too, but that''s not really under you control!', '2002-11-25 13:50:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(160030, 8724, 327, '<td valign="top">I don''t agree but will put that aside and say the shot is pretty good. The perspective could of been a bit improved and the crop on the bottom is not even.<br/>Over all- nice job and on topic!  Justine</td>', 'I don''t agree but will put that aside and say the shot is pretty good. The perspective could of been a bit improved and the crop on the bottom is not even.Over all- nice job and on topic!  Justine', '2002-11-25 15:12:00.000000', NULL, 1),
