(160689, 8773, 5121, '<td valign="top">Yeah, but he seems to be enjoying himself.  Nice colourful pic.</td>', 'Yeah, but he seems to be enjoying himself.  Nice colourful pic.', '2002-12-01 07:38:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(160690, 8773, 811, '<td valign="top">you have done well at filling the frame with your subject, and I like the almost triangle formed with his body and arms.  That gives the picture a well-balanced look, I think.  This angle works well, though my first impression was that you probably should have tried another.  The sign in the background was my only clue that this was not an American theme park or something (well, that, and this young man doesn''t have on a cheesy uniform), so it is important that it is visible, I think, as the meaning of your picture can change across the ocean.<br/><br/>The lighting is good, as is the focus, in that the subject is well focused.  The color are nice, but I am wondering if the "negative" feeling that your title conveys wouldn''t better be expressed in black and white.  It may also help to emphasize the subject by "downplaying" the other "stuff" in the background.  I played around with it some in PaintShop and on my monitor, converting it to black and white, tweaking the contrast a bit, and running an unsharp mask made it a bit edgier and more definable, but that is just my personal taste.  <br/><br/>Overall, I felt that the shot was good, and that it fit the challenge well.  Good luck in the future.</td>', 'you have done well at filling the frame with your subject, and I like the almost triangle formed with his body and arms.  That gives the picture a well-balanced look, I think.  This angle works well, though my first impression was that you probably should have tried another.  The sign in the background was my only clue that this was not an American theme park or something (well, that, and this young man doesn''t have on a cheesy uniform), so it is important that it is visible, I think, as the meaning of your picture can change across the ocean.The lighting is good, as is the focus, in that the subject is well focused.  The color are nice, but I am wondering if the "negative" feeling that your title conveys wouldn''t better be expressed in black and white.  It may also help to emphasize the subject by "downplaying" the other "stuff" in the background.  I played around with it some in PaintShop and on my monitor, converting it to black and white, tweaking the contrast a bit, and running an unsharp mask made it a bit edgier and more definable, but that is just my personal taste.  Overall, I felt that the shot was good, and that it fit the challenge well.  Good luck in the future.', '2002-12-03 16:20:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(160691, 8773, 640, '<td valign="top">Interesting how most of the comments centered around the title. I do agree, I chose a bad one. For those interested, this was shot in a park outside of Bangkok. His wages are incredibly low, but its all relative, as the cost of living is also very low. I do appreciate all your comments--even the ones that hurt (my pride)!</td>', 'Interesting how most of the comments centered around the title. I do agree, I chose a bad one. For those interested, this was shot in a park outside of Bangkok. His wages are incredibly low, but its all relative, as the cost of living is also very low. I do appreciate all your comments--even the ones that hurt (my pride)!', '2002-12-03 22:13:00.000000', NULL, 0),
