(161145, 8805, 2170, '<td valign="top">Great action shot!  A little dark, but otherwise perfect for this challenge.  muckpond</td>', 'Great action shot!  A little dark, but otherwise perfect for this challenge.  muckpond', '2002-11-29 11:31:00.000000', NULL, 1);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(161146, 8805, 4596, '<td valign="top">Great action shot in this telephoto shot. Good detail. 9 of 10.</td>', 'Great action shot in this telephoto shot. Good detail. 9 of 10.', '2002-11-30 12:01:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161147, 8805, 4055, '<td valign="top">Lovely shot but a bit yellow for my taste. Good composition and the focus for this kind of shot is OK. High score from Sweden (Just because we have so many good swimmers, ha ha). /carsten</td>', 'Lovely shot but a bit yellow for my taste. Good composition and the focus for this kind of shot is OK. High score from Sweden (Just because we have so many good swimmers, ha ha). /carsten', '2002-11-30 12:22:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161148, 8805, 4411, '<td valign="top">Nice action shot. A bit noisy but I guess light was in short supply. Well done.</td>', 'Nice action shot. A bit noisy but I guess light was in short supply. Well done.', '2002-11-30 20:33:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161149, 8805, 3730, '<td valign="top">Excellent capture...love the framing...great timing...wish the water splash was a bit sharper...9 - zadore</td>', 'Excellent capture...love the framing...great timing...wish the water splash was a bit sharper...9 - zadore', '2002-12-01 09:44:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161150, 8805, 3279, '<td valign="top">This to me is real front page stuff - well framed and with the splashing water frozen nicely. Slightly noisy image (especially visible on the Omega board in the background) but it doesn''t really detract from the shot. Nice!</td>', 'This to me is real front page stuff - well framed and with the splashing water frozen nicely. Slightly noisy image (especially visible on the Omega board in the background) but it doesn''t really detract from the shot. Nice!', '2002-12-01 16:11:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161151, 8805, 3087, '<td valign="top">8, Kavey</td>', '8, Kavey', '2002-12-01 16:26:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161152, 8805, 806, '<td valign="top">Great catch. These are particularly hard to get as the water usually consumes the subject. Great expression on the subject.. perfect timing on your part.</td>', 'Great catch. These are particularly hard to get as the water usually consumes the subject. Great expression on the subject.. perfect timing on your part.', '2002-12-01 22:52:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161153, 8805, 3102, '<td valign="top">Very well done!  I like the way you were able to capture his face in sharp focus while the surrounding water movement is blurred.  Beautiful!</td>', 'Very well done!  I like the way you were able to capture his face in sharp focus while the surrounding water movement is blurred.  Beautiful!', '2002-12-01 23:45:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161154, 8805, 2352, '<td valign="top">I can feel the splash!  Congrats!</td>', 'I can feel the splash!  Congrats!', '2002-12-02 01:02:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(161155, 8805, 2667, '<td valign="top">Cograts Arnit, excellent action shot!</td>', 'Cograts Arnit, excellent action shot!', '2002-12-02 11:58:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(161156, 8805, 5121, '<td valign="top">Congrats.</td>', 'Congrats.', '2002-12-02 13:59:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(161157, 8805, 3540, '<td valign="top">Composition - The first thing I think of looking at this shot is the framing which is exemplary.  The focal point of this picture is in the perfect spot.  The capture of the face openly visible is excellent.  The focus on the face is great.  At the shutter speed used, it is amazing.  Even without the smile it is a great capture.  The lane boundary and swim cap colors are brilliant.  This image is definitely meeting the challenge.<br/><br/>Background - The background isn''t distracting from the image at all and is not wasted space with a "splash" of yellow on the wall.  The background is well out of focus as is expected in this type of shot.<br/><br/>Camera Technique - The shortcomings of this shot, if any, are in the camera techniques, most of which are out of the photographer''s control.  This shot desperately needs a very powerful flash that could reach 40M and blind half the crowd to make the shot any better.  The 1600 ISO has added a lot of graininess to the picture.  The slow shutter speed makes the water around the swimmer very blurry.  I''m very sure that the photographer did everything possible to use the available light to make the shot as good as it is.  I wish I took it :)<br/><br/>Processing - I don''t know if much was done to this shot.  I don''t see anything that looks obviously processed into the pic aside from boosting sats a bit to make the colors stand out more.  From what I can see here, I''m assuming it didn''t need much done to it.<br/><br/>Overall - The photographer really made the most of this opportunity for a great shot.  The graininess of the shot and the lack of focus, although understandable, do take something away from the shot.  In my mind it is still one of the best captures from this challenge, whether the voters said it was or not.  Congrats on a fantastic shot Arnit - Inspzil<br/><br/></td>', 'Composition - The first thing I think of looking at this shot is the framing which is exemplary.  The focal point of this picture is in the perfect spot.  The capture of the face openly visible is excellent.  The focus on the face is great.  At the shutter speed used, it is amazing.  Even without the smile it is a great capture.  The lane boundary and swim cap colors are brilliant.  This image is definitely meeting the challenge.Background - The background isn''t distracting from the image at all and is not wasted space with a "splash" of yellow on the wall.  The background is well out of focus as is expected in this type of shot.Camera Technique - The shortcomings of this shot, if any, are in the camera techniques, most of which are out of the photographer''s control.  This shot desperately needs a very powerful flash that could reach 40M and blind half the crowd to make the shot any better.  The 1600 ISO has added a lot of graininess to the picture.  The slow shutter speed makes the water around the swimmer very blurry.  I''m very sure that the photographer did everything possible to use the available light to make the shot as good as it is.  I wish I took it :)Processing - I don''t know if much was done to this shot.  I don''t see anything that looks obviously processed into the pic aside from boosting sats a bit to make the colors stand out more.  From what I can see here, I''m assuming it didn''t need much done to it.Overall - The photographer really made the most of this opportunity for a great shot.  The graininess of the shot and the lack of focus, although understandable, do take something away from the shot.  In my mind it is still one of the best captures from this challenge, whether the voters said it was or not.  Congrats on a fantastic shot Arnit - Inspzil', '2002-12-03 23:54:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(161158, 8807, 4967, '<td valign="top">Good idea, but needs a human element to be front page news.</td>', 'Good idea, but needs a human element to be front page news.', '2002-11-25 01:15:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161159, 8807, 327, '<td valign="top">IMPACT + here. The b&amp;w makes it even stronger. Good eye. Justine</td>', 'IMPACT + here. The b&w makes it even stronger. Good eye. Justine', '2002-11-25 16:27:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161160, 8807, 772, '<td valign="top">I''m curious why you chose black and white on this image?  I would think that there is some interesting color here... I think a lower camera perspective here could be nice also :) - Please help us enhance this site that we all enjoy by commenting on photos each week.  The photographers really appreciate it :) - setzler</td>', 'I''m curious why you chose black and white on this image?  I would think that there is some interesting color here... I think a lower camera perspective here could be nice also :) - Please help us enhance this site that we all enjoy by commenting on photos each week.  The photographers really appreciate it :) - setzler', '2002-11-26 14:48:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161161, 8807, 4514, '<td valign="top">Wow this is a tear jerker.  Sorry to say. Good Job.  Not because it is a great shot but I am sorry about the Children.  :-(</td>', 'Wow this is a tear jerker.  Sorry to say. Good Job.  Not because it is a great shot but I am sorry about the Children.  :-(', '2002-11-27 05:59:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161162, 8807, 543, '<td valign="top">B/W is somewhat appropriate to the mood of your image, but I don''t think it works with the subject.  A tighter composition would also help.  I''m interested to hear the rest of this tragic story.</td>', 'B/W is somewhat appropriate to the mood of your image, but I don''t think it works with the subject.  A tighter composition would also help.  I''m interested to hear the rest of this tragic story.', '2002-11-28 13:12:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161163, 8807, 5158, '<td valign="top">For sure the hardest picture of the whole challenge. Brings me back from the joy and fun of the challenge to the real world and its cruelty. Hard to vote, but still thumb up.</td>', 'For sure the hardest picture of the whole challenge. Brings me back from the joy and fun of the challenge to the real world and its cruelty. Hard to vote, but still thumb up.', '2002-11-28 17:14:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161164, 8807, 2170, '<td valign="top">I think this would be more effective if shot from an angle.  Shot dead-on like this makes it feel more like a snapshot and less like a "photograph."  *shrug*  Just a suggestion.  muckpond</td>', 'I think this would be more effective if shot from an angle.  Shot dead-on like this makes it feel more like a snapshot and less like a "photograph."  *shrug*  Just a suggestion.  muckpond', '2002-11-30 16:46:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161165, 8807, 4648, '<td valign="top">Should have been in soft color.  Would make the messages on the wal stand out, as well as the heart felt things left there.  This doesn''t impace in B&amp;W.  You''ve got to get their attention to get them to read the article.  Otherwise technically good photo.  PTL6</td>', 'Should have been in soft color.  Would make the messages on the wal stand out, as well as the heart felt things left there.  This doesn''t impace in B&W.  You''ve got to get their attention to get them to read the article.  Otherwise technically good photo.  PTL6', '2002-11-30 20:23:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161166, 8807, 656, '<td valign="top">It is a sad story and your picture reflects it well.   The black and white does add to the feel.  Perhaps if you had taken the picture from a lower (more child-like) perspective you could have further accentuated the mood of the picture ?   The background wall/ panels are slightly tilted which seems to be accidental and would be worth fixing by a slight rotation. <br/><br/>I find the balloon very centered in the frame - maybe moving it off center would have provided a more flowing composition - eye starting at the balloon, moving down and across the other memorial pieces.  as it is I get stuck at the balloon and don''t really look elsewhere.  Hope this is useful for you.</td>', 'It is a sad story and your picture reflects it well.   The black and white does add to the feel.  Perhaps if you had taken the picture from a lower (more child-like) perspective you could have further accentuated the mood of the picture ?   The background wall/ panels are slightly tilted which seems to be accidental and would be worth fixing by a slight rotation. I find the balloon very centered in the frame - maybe moving it off center would have provided a more flowing composition - eye starting at the balloon, moving down and across the other memorial pieces.  as it is I get stuck at the balloon and don''t really look elsewhere.  Hope this is useful for you.', '2002-12-03 15:52:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(161167, 8808, 3280, '<td valign="top">Very nice color and clarity, the angle on the "Town Hall" seems a bit severe though. DPz</td>', 'Very nice color and clarity, the angle on the "Town Hall" seems a bit severe though. DPz', '2002-11-25 00:29:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161168, 8808, 327, '<td valign="top">Very pretty,......love the perspective, colors. Nice work. Justine</td>', 'Very pretty,......love the perspective, colors. Nice work. Justine', '2002-11-25 16:30:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161169, 8808, 4851, '<td valign="top">I like the angle. Great colours.</td>', 'I like the angle. Great colours.', '2002-11-26 11:38:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161170, 8808, 1826, '<td valign="top">I like this perspective. Kaz</td>', 'I like this perspective. Kaz', '2002-11-26 14:10:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161171, 8808, 3018, '<td valign="top">Nice composition.</td>', 'Nice composition.', '2002-11-26 18:41:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161172, 8808, 2279, '<td valign="top">I love the colors and the angle of this shot. Good job. 9. byetko.</td>', 'I love the colors and the angle of this shot. Good job. 9. byetko.', '2002-11-27 00:11:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161173, 8808, 4514, '<td valign="top">Great shot.  Caught the idea.</td>', 'Great shot.  Caught the idea.', '2002-11-27 02:03:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161174, 8808, 2170, '<td valign="top">The red bulb that is kind of the focus of the picture is somewhat obstructed and dark.  But this shot has great framing and definitely tells a story.  The sky is beautiful, too -- my absolute favorite color.  muckpond</td>', 'The red bulb that is kind of the focus of the picture is somewhat obstructed and dark.  But this shot has great framing and definitely tells a story.  The sky is beautiful, too -- my absolute favorite color.  muckpond', '2002-11-27 10:14:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161175, 8808, 2490, '<td valign="top">Only problem here is that the only things that look festive are the balls on the tree.  The rest of the shot has a much more serious tone.  6 nards656</td>', 'Only problem here is that the only things that look festive are the balls on the tree.  The rest of the shot has a much more serious tone.  6 nards656', '2002-11-27 21:07:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161176, 8808, 3540, '<td valign="top">Wonderful color in the sky.  The bulbs are too dark and hidden.  They should really stand out for this shot.  This building isn''t the greatest subject either.  It looks a little run down to be a cheery xmas shot. - Inspzil</td>', 'Wonderful color in the sky.  The bulbs are too dark and hidden.  They should really stand out for this shot.  This building isn''t the greatest subject either.  It looks a little run down to be a cheery xmas shot. - Inspzil', '2002-11-29 04:39:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161177, 8808, 714, '<td valign="top">Very, very nice photo.  Great DOF.  Vote 10 Sonifo</td>', 'Very, very nice photo.  Great DOF.  Vote 10 Sonifo', '2002-11-29 19:50:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161178, 8808, 4596, '<td valign="top">Okay shot. Good composition. Photo journalism? Perhaps.</td>', 'Okay shot. Good composition. Photo journalism? Perhaps.', '2002-11-30 17:25:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161179, 8808, 4648, '<td valign="top">I personally don''t feel that 4 little Christmas balls, one so hidden I almost missed it, is not festive.  Good idea but poor execution.  Decent  picture but doesn''t cause me to want to see any more pictures, much less read the article.  Picture looks took crowded.  Should have zoomed back - would have uncrowded or uncluttered pic, and might have shown some festiveness.  PTL5</td>', 'I personally don''t feel that 4 little Christmas balls, one so hidden I almost missed it, is not festive.  Good idea but poor execution.  Decent  picture but doesn''t cause me to want to see any more pictures, much less read the article.  Picture looks took crowded.  Should have zoomed back - would have uncrowded or uncluttered pic, and might have shown some festiveness.  PTL5', '2002-11-30 20:28:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161180, 8808, 2221, '<td valign="top">You must live in the southern hemisphere. I envy you for that blue sky and the sun *sniff* ;-) A well done photo. I like the angle and the placement of the objects. -stephan</td>', 'You must live in the southern hemisphere. I envy you for that blue sky and the sun *sniff* ;-) A well done photo. I like the angle and the placement of the objects. -stephan', '2002-12-01 10:14:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161181, 8808, 2, '<td valign="top">Cool shot, and nice bright, vivid colors.</td>', 'Cool shot, and nice bright, vivid colors.', '2002-12-01 23:17:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161182, 8808, 3540, '<td valign="top">Composition - My first impression of this pic was that the building was looking a little rough.  I didn''t like the contrast that provided between it and the bulbs in the tree.  The top of the building looks singed.  The second thing I noticed was that the bulbs are a little underexposed.  Nothing major though there.  The third thing I noticed was that this is a great great camera angle to take this picture.  It includes a nice balance of tree on one side and building on the other.  The building does offer some nice contrasts itself in the forms of circles and straight lines.  Christmas bulbs look odd to me without any snow.<br/><br/>Background - Very nice rich color in the sky.  Its a little too blue though to the point of looking fake.  I personally don''t mind that at all.  There really isn''t much else to consider for background, so lets move on.<br/><br/>Camera work - The strongest thing here is the angle the picture was shot.  The DOF is really good for the composition of this shot.  The bulbs being a little dark might be tough to fix and maybe just as tough to process within the limits of the rules.  Strong camera work!  (I''ve been considering buying the model of camera you have)<br/><br/>Post processing - I can''t see anything too out of the ordinary, so that''s a good sign.  <br/><br/>Overall - I generally like the shot.  I think it would be found in a newspaper somewhere, although maybe not the front page.  I would''ve liked to see a newer building but this older one will work.  - Bob (Inspzil)<br/></td>', 'Composition - My first impression of this pic was that the building was looking a little rough.  I didn''t like the contrast that provided between it and the bulbs in the tree.  The top of the building looks singed.  The second thing I noticed was that the bulbs are a little underexposed.  Nothing major though there.  The third thing I noticed was that this is a great great camera angle to take this picture.  It includes a nice balance of tree on one side and building on the other.  The building does offer some nice contrasts itself in the forms of circles and straight lines.  Christmas bulbs look odd to me without any snow.Background - Very nice rich color in the sky.  Its a little too blue though to the point of looking fake.  I personally don''t mind that at all.  There really isn''t much else to consider for background, so lets move on.Camera work - The strongest thing here is the angle the picture was shot.  The DOF is really good for the composition of this shot.  The bulbs being a little dark might be tough to fix and maybe just as tough to process within the limits of the rules.  Strong camera work!  (I''ve been considering buying the model of camera you have)Post processing - I can''t see anything too out of the ordinary, so that''s a good sign.  Overall - I generally like the shot.  I think it would be found in a newspaper somewhere, although maybe not the front page.  I would''ve liked to see a newer building but this older one will work.  - Bob (Inspzil)', '2002-12-03 23:50:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(161183, 8810, 4967, '<td valign="top">Very cute, and defiitiely news for DPC the magazine!  :-)  Good idea.</td>', 'Very cute, and defiitiely news for DPC the magazine!  :-)  Good idea.', '2002-11-25 01:36:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161184, 8810, 4210, '<td valign="top">Very very cute.</td>', 'Very very cute.', '2002-11-25 02:43:00.000000', NULL, 1),
