(161324, 8816, 5390, '<td valign="top"><br/>Great composition - contrast</td>', 'Great composition - contrast', '2002-11-26 16:51:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161325, 8816, 3416, '<td valign="top">In my opinion it is the best image of the week, adjusts to the subject, a perfect frame and those glances that introduce to me in the message of I title. 9 jcof.</td>', 'In my opinion it is the best image of the week, adjusts to the subject, a perfect frame and those glances that introduce to me in the message of I title. 9 jcof.', '2002-11-26 17:54:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161326, 8816, 4162, '<td valign="top">The quality of this shot is great, its incredibly crisp clear! The expressions are great and the picture tells a story, but the title doesnt seem to fit the mood of the shot! So far, this is the only shot that I have thought should win.  Good Luck Natasha</td>', 'The quality of this shot is great, its incredibly crisp clear! The expressions are great and the picture tells a story, but the title doesnt seem to fit the mood of the shot! So far, this is the only shot that I have thought should win.  Good Luck Natasha', '2002-11-26 20:24:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161327, 8816, 3447, '<td valign="top">This is a stunning photograph!  Marvelous clarity and expression. A very solid 9.    JEM   Looked again - true photojournalism!   10  JEM</td>', 'This is a stunning photograph!  Marvelous clarity and expression. A very solid 9.    JEM   Looked again - true photojournalism!   10  JEM', '2002-11-26 20:25:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161328, 8816, 2337, '<td valign="top">Some here may be too young to fully understand the referance here, but be assured, someone got it :)  Great focus and wonderful exposure! ~ MyQyl ~</td>', 'Some here may be too young to fully understand the referance here, but be assured, someone got it :)  Great focus and wonderful exposure! ~ MyQyl ~', '2002-11-26 21:30:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161329, 8816, 4615, '<td valign="top">Hard to rate your photo and not the girl  (a 10 by the way)  What is the success story?</td>', 'Hard to rate your photo and not the girl  (a 10 by the way)  What is the success story?', '2002-11-26 21:59:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161330, 8816, 1670, '<td valign="top">One word: incredible. Image quality could of been a bit better though, but it deserves a 9.</td>', 'One word: incredible. Image quality could of been a bit better though, but it deserves a 9.', '2002-11-26 22:59:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161331, 8816, 3900, '<td valign="top">I''m not sure how you mean about the city being united.  Blacks and whites sit together all the time on public transportation, but they ignore each other just like whites ignore whites and blacks ignore blacks.  Public trans just isn''t the place to socialize now is it. Anyway, it''s a good shot...maybe a bit jaggy...too much sharpen maybe?</td>', 'I''m not sure how you mean about the city being united.  Blacks and whites sit together all the time on public transportation, but they ignore each other just like whites ignore whites and blacks ignore blacks.  Public trans just isn''t the place to socialize now is it. Anyway, it''s a good shot...maybe a bit jaggy...too much sharpen maybe?', '2002-11-27 03:17:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161332, 8816, 772, '<td valign="top">Congrats on an excellent photo... I love the composition... the guy with the hood ''makes'' this photo since he''s looking right at you.  That''s a great catch :)  I''m giving this photo a 10, but I still have some issues with the overall image quality.  I''m not sure what my issues here are, but the image could possibly oversharpened.  Something just looks a bit strange about it.  Maybe the contrast is a little high also?  Contrast is important to me in a b/w image though... great shot :) - setzler</td>', 'Congrats on an excellent photo... I love the composition... the guy with the hood ''makes'' this photo since he''s looking right at you.  That''s a great catch :)  I''m giving this photo a 10, but I still have some issues with the overall image quality.  I''m not sure what my issues here are, but the image could possibly oversharpened.  Something just looks a bit strange about it.  Maybe the contrast is a little high also?  Contrast is important to me in a b/w image though... great shot :) - setzler', '2002-11-27 07:56:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161333, 8816, 1019, '<td valign="top">Good contrasts of subject good composition--andrewm</td>', 'Good contrasts of subject good composition--andrewm', '2002-11-27 12:18:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161334, 8816, 3459, '<td valign="top">The expressions on the faces are great, the whole image makes a point.  While I think the contrast might have been pushed a bit too far, it does not take away much.  Very well seen, congratulations!</td>', 'The expressions on the faces are great, the whole image makes a point.  While I think the contrast might have been pushed a bit too far, it does not take away much.  Very well seen, congratulations!', '2002-11-27 13:45:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161335, 8816, 3306, '<td valign="top">I like this picture. Very Candid. Good job. Lnede</td>', 'I like this picture. Very Candid. Good job. Lnede', '2002-11-27 21:30:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161336, 8816, 5347, '<td valign="top">you just think she is hot!... well your right :)</td>', 'you just think she is hot!... well your right :)', '2002-11-27 23:18:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161337, 8816, 5411, '<td valign="top">Beautiful clarity, nice composition,  evokes emotion.</td>', 'Beautiful clarity, nice composition,  evokes emotion.', '2002-11-28 01:34:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161338, 8816, 5212, '<td valign="top">Excellent photo, right on topic, makes a strong statement.</td>', 'Excellent photo, right on topic, makes a strong statement.', '2002-11-28 01:52:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161339, 8816, 543, '<td valign="top">I been caught shootin'' man.  Looks a little oversharp from where I sit, and could use just a touch of + gamma.  Then again, I like the way the guy''s face looms out of the blackness in his hood.  Nicely done.</td>', 'I been caught shootin'' man.  Looks a little oversharp from where I sit, and could use just a touch of + gamma.  Then again, I like the way the guy''s face looms out of the blackness in his hood.  Nicely done.', '2002-11-28 13:22:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161340, 8816, 4648, '<td valign="top">Over sharpened jumps out at me - her hair, scarf, and brochure &amp; book.  Like the little girl behind her on her left.  She almost looks afraid and the guy with her looks suspicious of you.  Great depth to their eyes and expressions.  Good photo just wish you hadn''t sharpened it.  Maybe lightened and adjusted the contrast instead.  I try both to see which is better.  Just my thoughts.  PTL6</td>', 'Over sharpened jumps out at me - her hair, scarf, and brochure & book.  Like the little girl behind her on her left.  She almost looks afraid and the guy with her looks suspicious of you.  Great depth to their eyes and expressions.  Good photo just wish you hadn''t sharpened it.  Maybe lightened and adjusted the contrast instead.  I try both to see which is better.  Just my thoughts.  PTL6', '2002-11-28 21:19:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161341, 8816, 3317, '<td valign="top">too bad there are so many vertical bars on subways, eh? why black and white? this looks kinda colorful</td>', 'too bad there are so many vertical bars on subways, eh? why black and white? this looks kinda colorful', '2002-11-28 21:39:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161342, 8816, 5044, '<td valign="top">Nice composition. Could have stood alittle more exposure. Man''s face has too many shadows, IMO. I still like the shot very much. Captures the essence of the challenge.</td>', 'Nice composition. Could have stood alittle more exposure. Man''s face has too many shadows, IMO. I still like the shot very much. Captures the essence of the challenge.', '2002-11-29 13:04:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161343, 8816, 5121, '<td valign="top">Well taken, good and sharp.  Superb!</td>', 'Well taken, good and sharp.  Superb!', '2002-11-30 15:01:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161344, 8816, 2170, '<td valign="top">This is a great photo.  Has it been sharpened?  The whole shot seems jagged, which is unsettling.  This is really an excellent photo, though.  muckpond</td>', 'This is a great photo.  Has it been sharpened?  The whole shot seems jagged, which is unsettling.  This is really an excellent photo, though.  muckpond', '2002-11-30 16:47:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161345, 8816, 4596, '<td valign="top">Subject of photo appears to create a different feeling than the title conveys.</td>', 'Subject of photo appears to create a different feeling than the title conveys.', '2002-11-30 17:09:00.000000', NULL, 1);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(161346, 8816, 3247, '<td valign="top">Needs to be rotated CW. Great DOF.  Her face is great.</td>', 'Needs to be rotated CW. Great DOF.  Her face is great.', '2002-11-30 17:58:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161347, 8816, 3380, '<td valign="top">I could really see this being published. Excellent job; great focus, lighting, and overall composition.</td>', 'I could really see this being published. Excellent job; great focus, lighting, and overall composition.', '2002-12-01 18:26:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161348, 8816, 3540, '<td valign="top">Congrats on a great shot Mag!!  Good luck on the blue challenge - Bob<br/></td>', 'Congrats on a great shot Mag!!  Good luck on the blue challenge - Bob', '2002-12-02 00:16:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(161349, 8816, 4267, '<td valign="top">great shot mag... it kept getting better each time I saw it... curious, did you ask for their permission to take the photo? or did ya just shoot it? let us know... thanks!<br/>~jeff</td>', 'great shot mag... it kept getting better each time I saw it... curious, did you ask for their permission to take the photo? or did ya just shoot it? let us know... thanks!~jeff', '2002-12-02 01:42:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(161350, 8816, 2792, '<td valign="top">Great job Kollin!</td>', 'Great job Kollin!', '2002-12-02 07:39:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(161351, 8816, 472, '<td valign="top">i just took it.. im pretty bold with the stealth (oxymoron?)  : ) .. my only own personal gripe was that i had to shoot at high iso and it was sharp but grainy. so i ran it through a noise reduction and it made it really soft and weird.. sharpening just made it more weird.  still i think it would have done worse grainy. :P maybe i''ll post it ..</td>', 'i just took it.. im pretty bold with the stealth (oxymoron?)  : ) .. my only own personal gripe was that i had to shoot at high iso and it was sharp but grainy. so i ran it through a noise reduction and it made it really soft and weird.. sharpening just made it more weird.  still i think it would have done worse grainy. :P maybe i''ll post it ..', '2002-12-02 16:07:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(161352, 8816, 527, '<td valign="top">I think I would have left some of the grain in. Grain in candid or photojournalistic photos is acceptable. As iit is there is some plasticity that I find a little distracting. The photo is very successful, however, in large part because of the black male who''s looking straight at the camera contrasting with the beautiful white female who is absobed in her book. Even the little girl seems to be looking at the camera. There is a lot of visually contrasting relationships in this photo to make it very effective as a black and white. I think it is cropped just right with just enough information included to show these people in their environment. I love photos like this because it makes me wonder what everyone is thinking about and I start to imagine a story about them. Technically, I think it could be a little better but it is still a very engaging photo.<br/><br/>Tim Jensen</td>', 'I think I would have left some of the grain in. Grain in candid or photojournalistic photos is acceptable. As iit is there is some plasticity that I find a little distracting. The photo is very successful, however, in large part because of the black male who''s looking straight at the camera contrasting with the beautiful white female who is absobed in her book. Even the little girl seems to be looking at the camera. There is a lot of visually contrasting relationships in this photo to make it very effective as a black and white. I think it is cropped just right with just enough information included to show these people in their environment. I love photos like this because it makes me wonder what everyone is thinking about and I start to imagine a story about them. Technically, I think it could be a little better but it is still a very engaging photo.Tim Jensen', '2002-12-03 00:02:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(161353, 8816, 472, '<td valign="top">i agree with tim that grain is accepable lots of kinds of shots, but this is dpc we''re talking about : ) .. So I played it ''safe''.  anyway, here''s the shot without noise reduction added.  <br/><br/>//www.pbase.com/image/8309856<br/><br/></td>', 'i agree with tim that grain is accepable lots of kinds of shots, but this is dpc we''re talking about : ) .. So I played it ''safe''.  anyway, here''s the shot without noise reduction added.  //www.pbase.com/image/8309856', '2002-12-03 19:21:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(161354, 8816, 1280, '<td valign="top">My first impression when I saw this image is that it is cropped a little too tight.  I''d like to see some head-room above the subjects. Aside from that the composition is good, including just enough background.   Looking beyond that I see two beautiful teenaged faces, and a kid peeking over. The faces are a pleasant subject and you successfully managed to expose different skintones beautifully. .   That is a difficult thing to do...good job!  The dark skinned young man is partially shaded due to his visor and hood, but that works just fine.<br/>Post-processing worked out ok.  I think it was a wise choice to remove the grain.  I should have done that with mine. <br/>Overall it''s a good picture, and would fit in the newspaper.  <br/>Grayce<br/><br/></td>', 'My first impression when I saw this image is that it is cropped a little too tight.  I''d like to see some head-room above the subjects. Aside from that the composition is good, including just enough background.   Looking beyond that I see two beautiful teenaged faces, and a kid peeking over. The faces are a pleasant subject and you successfully managed to expose different skintones beautifully. .   That is a difficult thing to do...good job!  The dark skinned young man is partially shaded due to his visor and hood, but that works just fine.Post-processing worked out ok.  I think it was a wise choice to remove the grain.  I should have done that with mine. Overall it''s a good picture, and would fit in the newspaper.  Grayce', '2002-12-03 23:16:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(161355, 8817, 4267, '<td valign="top">oh, hitting below the belt with cuteness! not fair! :o)</td>', 'oh, hitting below the belt with cuteness! not fair! :o)', '2002-11-25 01:18:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161356, 8817, 3127, '<td valign="top">This kitty looks like one of mine. Good pic.</td>', 'This kitty looks like one of mine. Good pic.', '2002-11-25 10:53:00.000000', NULL, 1),
