(161758, 8841, 3317, '<td valign="top">the light''s hitting the guy in the center just perfect, you caught him at just the right time, too bad to get the faces you gotta light meter the sky out of the picture. fits the challenge to a tee, way to go out somewhere exciting, make a picture happen.</td>', 'the light''s hitting the guy in the center just perfect, you caught him at just the right time, too bad to get the faces you gotta light meter the sky out of the picture. fits the challenge to a tee, way to go out somewhere exciting, make a picture happen.', '2002-11-28 21:54:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161759, 8841, 2829, '<td valign="top">I think this is the best photo out of all the entries. It captures the moment very well and the surroundings give you all the information you need to determine what they are there for. Well captured.</td>', 'I think this is the best photo out of all the entries. It captures the moment very well and the surroundings give you all the information you need to determine what they are there for. Well captured.', '2002-11-29 14:04:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161760, 8841, 2752, '<td valign="top">Great photojournalism shot.  I can feel the pulse of the crowd.</td>', 'Great photojournalism shot.  I can feel the pulse of the crowd.', '2002-11-30 16:57:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161761, 8841, 4648, '<td valign="top">Your singular title puzzled me until the photo finished scrolling down.  But, you are right - only the one !man in the middle, and maybe the man in the bottom left corner, is the only one who seems to be fired up about this.  And he has great emotion showing on his face.  The man and woman behind him seem to be having a good fun time.  The others seem uninvolved, just there.  If you look at the man in the lower left corner you''ll see his head is turned more downward and his eyebrow and forhead show no emotion, only has his hand raised in support.  Maybe your title fits your picture more than you realized - singular.  Good photo.  Nice job.  PTL6</td>', 'Your singular title puzzled me until the photo finished scrolling down.  But, you are right - only the one !man in the middle, and maybe the man in the bottom left corner, is the only one who seems to be fired up about this.  And he has great emotion showing on his face.  The man and woman behind him seem to be having a good fun time.  The others seem uninvolved, just there.  If you look at the man in the lower left corner you''ll see his head is turned more downward and his eyebrow and forhead show no emotion, only has his hand raised in support.  Maybe your title fits your picture more than you realized - singular.  Good photo.  Nice job.  PTL6', '2002-11-30 20:38:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161762, 8841, 2170, '<td valign="top">An excellent photograph -- definitely a winner.  Full of captured emotion and perfectly crisp and clear.  This is a stand-out submission.  muckpond</td>', 'An excellent photograph -- definitely a winner.  Full of captured emotion and perfectly crisp and clear.  This is a stand-out submission.  muckpond', '2002-11-30 23:30:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161763, 8841, 5121, '<td valign="top">Good piece of photojournalism!</td>', 'Good piece of photojournalism!', '2002-12-01 07:40:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161764, 8841, 3279, '<td valign="top">Nicely captures the emtions of the central figure seemingly shouting right into the camera. All the crowd seem to be converging on him too although it seems slightly out of place to have this angry central character and at least two smiling faces immediately to his right!</td>', 'Nicely captures the emtions of the central figure seemingly shouting right into the camera. All the crowd seem to be converging on him too although it seems slightly out of place to have this angry central character and at least two smiling faces immediately to his right!', '2002-12-01 16:14:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161765, 8841, 2716, '<td valign="top">Very photo journalistic :)  I like it.  Really conveys the emotions strongly.  Jacko. 9</td>', 'Very photo journalistic :)  I like it.  Really conveys the emotions strongly.  Jacko. 9', '2002-12-01 19:36:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161766, 8841, 806, '<td valign="top">Great catch. The exposure seems a little off to me - sky and sign blend together, yet there is a bit of blue sky in the upper right corner.</td>', 'Great catch. The exposure seems a little off to me - sky and sign blend together, yet there is a bit of blue sky in the upper right corner.', '2002-12-01 22:49:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161767, 8841, 3976, '<td valign="top">Thanks to those of you who voted.  This photo exhibited a lot of emotion.  It is quite thrilling to attend a political exhibition as such.  There are many different humanistic and atmospheric emotions that one can capture at such an event.  I plan to continue and suggest yall to try it as well if you havent already.</td>', 'Thanks to those of you who voted.  This photo exhibited a lot of emotion.  It is quite thrilling to attend a political exhibition as such.  There are many different humanistic and atmospheric emotions that one can capture at such an event.  I plan to continue and suggest yall to try it as well if you havent already.', '2002-12-02 01:31:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(161768, 8841, 737, '<td valign="top">(1) COMPOSITION (CONTENT) -  Very good. The subject is very relevant, and some version of this is always front-page news. The central figure certainly shows the emotion which is present with this subject. I like the slight blur on the hand  shows action and emotion.<br/>(2) BACKGROUND   two things hit me, perhaps both out of your control. First, the sky is overly bright. Probably a cloudy day with high overcast. Second, the man and woman just left of the elbow are smiling. Bad form for an emotional rally.  Perhaps a shot a minute later would have found them unsmiling.     On the other hand, I like the cropping  gives a good feeling of a crowd.<br/>(3) CAMERA WORK ,TECHNICAL  Focus and DOF look very good to me . No recommended changes.<br/>(4) DIGITAL PROCESSING ,TECHNICAL   For the challenge, no recommended changes. For publishing, Id try to darken the sky a tad.<br/>(5) MY OPINION ON THE PHOTO  When I first saw this photo, I thought  front page. It was made by the centered man who is yelling, and the subject.<br/><br/>Jim msp<br/>Critique Club<br/></td>', '(1) COMPOSITION (CONTENT) -  Very good. The subject is very relevant, and some version of this is always front-page news. The central figure certainly shows the emotion which is present with this subject. I like the slight blur on the hand  shows action and emotion.(2) BACKGROUND   two things hit me, perhaps both out of your control. First, the sky is overly bright. Probably a cloudy day with high overcast. Second, the man and woman just left of the elbow are smiling. Bad form for an emotional rally.  Perhaps a shot a minute later would have found them unsmiling.     On the other hand, I like the cropping  gives a good feeling of a crowd.(3) CAMERA WORK ,TECHNICAL  Focus and DOF look very good to me . No recommended changes.(4) DIGITAL PROCESSING ,TECHNICAL   For the challenge, no recommended changes. For publishing, Id try to darken the sky a tad.(5) MY OPINION ON THE PHOTO  When I first saw this photo, I thought  front page. It was made by the centered man who is yelling, and the subject.Jim mspCritique Club', '2002-12-02 20:37:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(161769, 8842, 3032, '<td valign="top">Great composition, nice colors, nice use of DOF.</td>', 'Great composition, nice colors, nice use of DOF.', '2002-11-25 11:27:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161770, 8842, 327, '<td valign="top">Pretty shooting, your lighting is very nice. Justine</td>', 'Pretty shooting, your lighting is very nice. Justine', '2002-11-25 17:54:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161771, 8842, 1280, '<td valign="top">I like this photo.  The ttle wouldn''t really be appropriate for a monthly magazine, but rather for a daily, since you are counting days here. But back to the photo....I like it very much, but it seems to be more appropriate for a card.  The colors are nice and I like the composition.  The dof is ok, but the more I look at it, the more I''d like to see the entire image in focus. My eyes just follow the balls back to the rear one, and if it was a clearly focused as the others it would be more pleasing, in this case.  Not that I always want to see the whole pic in focus,  just in this one.  :-)<br/>Good luck in the challenge!  Grayce aka Gracious</td>', 'I like this photo.  The ttle wouldn''t really be appropriate for a monthly magazine, but rather for a daily, since you are counting days here. But back to the photo....I like it very much, but it seems to be more appropriate for a card.  The colors are nice and I like the composition.  The dof is ok, but the more I look at it, the more I''d like to see the entire image in focus. My eyes just follow the balls back to the rear one, and if it was a clearly focused as the others it would be more pleasing, in this case.  Not that I always want to see the whole pic in focus,  just in this one.  :-)Good luck in the challenge!  Grayce aka Gracious', '2002-11-25 19:40:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161772, 8842, 4388, '<td valign="top">it could be a Vogue cover.  it would look more like a cover if it was portrait rather than landscape.  good lighting and exposure.</td>', 'it could be a Vogue cover.  it would look more like a cover if it was portrait rather than landscape.  good lighting and exposure.', '2002-11-25 21:44:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161773, 8842, 1143, '<td valign="top">Great technique. This would work for christmas cards. Nice color choices and great dof. Good job controlling the exposure. Those shiny tinsel things can be tough.  ~indi</td>', 'Great technique. This would work for christmas cards. Nice color choices and great dof. Good job controlling the exposure. Those shiny tinsel things can be tough.  ~indi', '2002-11-25 22:37:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161774, 8842, 2344, '<td valign="top">Well we know this is your image Gordon and I must say I like the idea. Not crazy about the composition but christmas is worthy of the news at this time of the year. The middle ball looks out of place.. maybe if its bottom was sticking out a little bit more. Anyhow I think everyone''s image should remain anonymous and since your image won on another website it leaves it up for discussion.. and that''s not necessarily right either.</td>', 'Well we know this is your image Gordon and I must say I like the idea. Not crazy about the composition but christmas is worthy of the news at this time of the year. The middle ball looks out of place.. maybe if its bottom was sticking out a little bit more. Anyhow I think everyone''s image should remain anonymous and since your image won on another website it leaves it up for discussion.. and that''s not necessarily right either.', '2002-11-26 07:16:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161775, 8842, 4906, '<td valign="top">Nice pic, Gordon.</td>', 'Nice pic, Gordon.', '2002-11-26 09:12:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161776, 8842, 3416, '<td valign="top">Great photo, excellent technical quality.  The illumination is surrounding.  Good work.</td>', 'Great photo, excellent technical quality.  The illumination is surrounding.  Good work.', '2002-11-26 17:56:00.000000', NULL, 1),
