(161942, 8851, 1280, '<td valign="top">I love nature shots and this one definetly documents an event.  The lighting is excellent and the split second capture is perfect. I wonder how a different crop would be.  I''m not sure I like the little bit of land showing above.  I took the liberty of editing a copy in PS to illustrate what I am talking about.  If you''d like to see it feel free to email me. I do realize my opinion is just that...only an opinion.<br/>All in all I really like this very much and am scoring high.  8  Good luck in the challenge.  Grayce</td>', 'I love nature shots and this one definetly documents an event.  The lighting is excellent and the split second capture is perfect. I wonder how a different crop would be.  I''m not sure I like the little bit of land showing above.  I took the liberty of editing a copy in PS to illustrate what I am talking about.  If you''d like to see it feel free to email me. I do realize my opinion is just that...only an opinion.All in all I really like this very much and am scoring high.  8  Good luck in the challenge.  Grayce', '2002-11-30 23:46:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161943, 8851, 3280, '<td valign="top">Very nice, how long did you have to shoot to get this?  It may have been better with the grass on the left cropped out.  Good job. DPz</td>', 'Very nice, how long did you have to shoot to get this?  It may have been better with the grass on the left cropped out.  Good job. DPz', '2002-12-01 06:22:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161944, 8851, 4411, '<td valign="top">Nice catch!<br/>Looks like light was in short supply here, which is a shame - the photo is a bit too dark. I guess a longer shutter would have resulted in a long blur instead of a fish though!<br/>A tighter crop may have improved the composition, as it is the fish is taking up too little of the shot.<br/>Well done, a great moment to capture.</td>', 'Nice catch!Looks like light was in short supply here, which is a shame - the photo is a bit too dark. I guess a longer shutter would have resulted in a long blur instead of a fish though!A tighter crop may have improved the composition, as it is the fish is taking up too little of the shot.Well done, a great moment to capture.', '2002-12-01 06:38:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161945, 8851, 4969, '<td valign="top">Talk about capturing the moment! I love it! 10<br/><br/></td>', 'Talk about capturing the moment! I love it! 10', '2002-12-01 22:55:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161946, 8851, 2, '<td valign="top">This could definitely be the cover of an outdoors magazine if it were a little closer.  A great shot, nonetheless.</td>', 'This could definitely be the cover of an outdoors magazine if it were a little closer.  A great shot, nonetheless.', '2002-12-01 23:14:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161947, 8851, 4162, '<td valign="top">Critique by Natasha<br/><br/>COMPOSITION- CONTENT<br/>The content of the picture is great, this could really be a good picture for a fishing magazine. Eyes are definitely drawn to the fish and the light on the fish helps it stand out in the picture.  The rule of thirds has been applied here and this adds to the shot.  After the fish, the eyes are drawn to the river bank, and although overall the composition is nice, I think that the river bank isnt needed here.  I agree with some of the comments here, a closer crop would have helped the composition, making the fish larger in the frame and excluding some of the extra detail. I think that the idea of making this a vertical crop is a good one, cut off the left of the picture, including the grass, a little bit off the right for balance and then concentrate on the fish, the falling water and then also the bank would add to the framing.<br/><br/>BACKGROUND<br/><br/>I think a lot that I have said in the composition applies here.  Although beautiful the background overpowers the point of the picture, being the fish. Decrease the size of the background and the fish will "jump out" even more! LOL.<br/><br/>CAMERA WORK-TECHNICAL<br/>The fast shutter speed here is great, it captures the fish cleanly and in focus, great work! The lighting on the fish and water is lovely, also the background lighting is clear.  I would imagine that the water here is pretty dark, hence the "dark" comments. However if you had increased contrast, I think that the water would have got blown out.<br/><br/>DIGITAL PROCESSING-TECHNICAL<br/>I think that you could play around with the contrast a little here, as some people have suggested, try cutting out the background and adding a bit more light.  Though, to be honest Ifeel that the lighting is very good here, the water has got a nice clean glow to it.<br/><br/>MY OPINION<br/>This is a great capture and a vey beautiful setting, I think some more cropping would enhance this shot a lot.  Perfect timing! I hope that this critique helps!</td>', 'Critique by NatashaCOMPOSITION- CONTENTThe content of the picture is great, this could really be a good picture for a fishing magazine. Eyes are definitely drawn to the fish and the light on the fish helps it stand out in the picture.  The rule of thirds has been applied here and this adds to the shot.  After the fish, the eyes are drawn to the river bank, and although overall the composition is nice, I think that the river bank isnt needed here.  I agree with some of the comments here, a closer crop would have helped the composition, making the fish larger in the frame and excluding some of the extra detail. I think that the idea of making this a vertical crop is a good one, cut off the left of the picture, including the grass, a little bit off the right for balance and then concentrate on the fish, the falling water and then also the bank would add to the framing.BACKGROUNDI think a lot that I have said in the composition applies here.  Although beautiful the background overpowers the point of the picture, being the fish. Decrease the size of the background and the fish will "jump out" even more! LOL.CAMERA WORK-TECHNICALThe fast shutter speed here is great, it captures the fish cleanly and in focus, great work! The lighting on the fish and water is lovely, also the background lighting is clear.  I would imagine that the water here is pretty dark, hence the "dark" comments. However if you had increased contrast, I think that the water would have got blown out.DIGITAL PROCESSING-TECHNICALI think that you could play around with the contrast a little here, as some people have suggested, try cutting out the background and adding a bit more light.  Though, to be honest Ifeel that the lighting is very good here, the water has got a nice clean glow to it.MY OPINIONThis is a great capture and a vey beautiful setting, I think some more cropping would enhance this shot a lot.  Perfect timing! I hope that this critique helps!', '2002-12-02 20:51:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(161948, 8852, 3280, '<td valign="top">Good color, not too sure about the title. The white strip on the left is a bit distracting.  Nice shot though. DPz</td>', 'Good color, not too sure about the title. The white strip on the left is a bit distracting.  Nice shot though. DPz', '2002-11-25 00:22:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161949, 8852, 3102, '<td valign="top">Really?  From a fountain...?  Hmmmmm....</td>', 'Really?  From a fountain...?  Hmmmmm....', '2002-11-25 10:58:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161950, 8852, 327, '<td valign="top">LoL good humor. Justine</td>', 'LoL good humor. Justine', '2002-11-25 15:09:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161951, 8852, 3900, '<td valign="top">HUH, I''m sure this is not scolding water.  What is this really about???</td>', 'HUH, I''m sure this is not scolding water.  What is this really about???', '2002-11-27 05:04:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161952, 8852, 4514, '<td valign="top">There is just lots wrong here.  Color is nice but there is no control.</td>', 'There is just lots wrong here.  Color is nice but there is no control.', '2002-11-27 05:50:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161953, 8852, 811, '<td valign="top">The colors in this shot are awesome.  What detracts primarily is the lack of focus on any one thing, I think.  Good composition and framing though.  karmat</td>', 'The colors in this shot are awesome.  What detracts primarily is the lack of focus on any one thing, I think.  Good composition and framing though.  karmat', '2002-11-27 13:09:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161954, 8852, 2490, '<td valign="top">Hmmm.  Not sure how the photo matches with the title, but I understand the water LOOKS hot.  Don''t see a real photojournalism idea, but I am voting largely quality this week and taking the challenge largely for granted.  6 nards656</td>', 'Hmmm.  Not sure how the photo matches with the title, but I understand the water LOOKS hot.  Don''t see a real photojournalism idea, but I am voting largely quality this week and taking the challenge largely for granted.  6 nards656', '2002-11-27 21:04:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161955, 8852, 3447, '<td valign="top">Would have been nice to see the entire fountain.  Great hot colors.   JEM</td>', 'Would have been nice to see the entire fountain.  Great hot colors.   JEM', '2002-11-29 10:41:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161956, 8852, 1202, '<td valign="top">Composition: Subject Placement, Cropping, Background7,<br/>Technical: Focus, Exposure, Lighting, Processing7,<br/>Appeal: Is it Interesting, Motivating, Etc.? 7,<br/>Total Averaged Rating7.   Autool<br/></td>', 'Composition: Subject Placement, Cropping, Background7,Technical: Focus, Exposure, Lighting, Processing7,Appeal: Is it Interesting, Motivating, Etc.? 7,Total Averaged Rating7.   Autool', '2002-11-30 09:32:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161957, 8852, 4648, '<td valign="top">Out of focus, maybe from over enhancing the colors.  Not sure.  Building look all washed out.  Very poorly executed.  PTL3</td>', 'Out of focus, maybe from over enhancing the colors.  Not sure.  Building look all washed out.  Very poorly executed.  PTL3', '2002-12-01 18:49:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161958, 8852, 2586, '<td valign="top">I just read your forum post about the Critique Club and that made me decide to comment on this picture. First of all, I commend you on a nice sense of creativity. That shines through even though you''re working with low-end equipment that hampers efforts towards a great image the way you visualize it. I like the title because the color of the water has gotten a feel of fire about it, i.e. more creativity there :) The background of the houses and the tree is quite interesting; you don''t have dof capability so have you to work with what you got; would have been nice otherwise to blur this a little. There are two things i find distracting: one is the letters of the advertisement near the house; it''s a little too prominent (again, you had no control over that). The other thing i found distracting is the greyish foreground of the fountain edge. I would have cropped that out and the picture would have given more focus on the water/fire that way. Imho, cropping it that way would enhance the visual interest of the overall image. Overall, good job in creativity and really that''s the most important part (a better camera will come some day). Regards, Journey</td>', 'I just read your forum post about the Critique Club and that made me decide to comment on this picture. First of all, I commend you on a nice sense of creativity. That shines through even though you''re working with low-end equipment that hampers efforts towards a great image the way you visualize it. I like the title because the color of the water has gotten a feel of fire about it, i.e. more creativity there :) The background of the houses and the tree is quite interesting; you don''t have dof capability so have you to work with what you got; would have been nice otherwise to blur this a little. There are two things i find distracting: one is the letters of the advertisement near the house; it''s a little too prominent (again, you had no control over that). The other thing i found distracting is the greyish foreground of the fountain edge. I would have cropped that out and the picture would have given more focus on the water/fire that way. Imho, cropping it that way would enhance the visual interest of the overall image. Overall, good job in creativity and really that''s the most important part (a better camera will come some day). Regards, Journey', '2002-12-03 14:46:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(161959, 8852, 3032, '<td valign="top">~~~~Critique Club Comment~~~~<br/><br/>*Composition (content)*<br/>Interesting composition. <br/>Good balance between the main subject and the background subject.<br/>Good horizontal portayal.<br/>The lights on the building in the background provide some light intensity balance with the light of the fountain at the right. It also gives some variancy in color; yellow-red vs blue white.<br/>The arches of the background-building and the water itself provide depth.<br/>I guess that the material in the bottom is a concrede edge from the fountain. This gives a frame to the bottom, it doesn''t leave the composition open at that end, which might be a good thing if anything beyond that isn''t interesting.<br/>Standing back more to capture more of the fountain and to do more with the rule of thirds might have made this better tough.<br/><br/>*Background*<br/>When you are able to control aperture, you migh have wanted to experiment with the settings to get only the fountain edge to edge in focus and blur the background. Focus on 1/3th from the bottom of the frame an try F5-F2.8<br/><br/>*Camera Work (Technical)*<br/>You don''t have much control, but fortunately the shutterspeed was slow enough to capture the motion of the water. That is a good thing.<br/>The whitebalance is slightly on the blue side, a better camera would have done a better job or provided better manual settings.<br/>Unfortunately the camera destroy''s alle sharpness and detail by very agressive jpeg compression (I talked to you about that earlier in the forums) and that is what ruins this picture for the viewer. It could also do with some exposure compensation experimentation.<br/><br/>*Digital Processing (technical)*<br/>It makes no sense to discuss this. Because of the agressive jpeg compression many post processing techniques will come out bad. It might help under the new rules to make your image smaller!!!!!! You are not limited to 640x480 I believe, but can also RESAMPLE (Lanczos / bibubic algoritm; try Irfanview if you don''t have an editor that can do that; DONT RESIZE, ALWAYS RESAMPLE!!!). That process might take some of the compression artefacts away and allow you to save at a higher compression level, close to 150kb. The small file might even allow for some sharpening without worsening the picture! Check the new rules about the file size and check the forums about resampling and saving.<br/><br/>*My opinion*<br/>This is a very interesting picture (seriously, I don''t say this to make you feel better), but it is ruined by the camera. I hope that the new rules allow you to post something of better quality, because your approach to photography is promising.</td>', '~~~~Critique Club Comment~~~~*Composition (content)*Interesting composition. Good balance between the main subject and the background subject.Good horizontal portayal.The lights on the building in the background provide some light intensity balance with the light of the fountain at the right. It also gives some variancy in color; yellow-red vs blue white.The arches of the background-building and the water itself provide depth.I guess that the material in the bottom is a concrede edge from the fountain. This gives a frame to the bottom, it doesn''t leave the composition open at that end, which might be a good thing if anything beyond that isn''t interesting.Standing back more to capture more of the fountain and to do more with the rule of thirds might have made this better tough.*Background*When you are able to control aperture, you migh have wanted to experiment with the settings to get only the fountain edge to edge in focus and blur the background. Focus on 1/3th from the bottom of the frame an try F5-F2.8*Camera Work (Technical)*You don''t have much control, but fortunately the shutterspeed was slow enough to capture the motion of the water. That is a good thing.The whitebalance is slightly on the blue side, a better camera would have done a better job or provided better manual settings.Unfortunately the camera destroy''s alle sharpness and detail by very agressive jpeg compression (I talked to you about that earlier in the forums) and that is what ruins this picture for the viewer. It could also do with some exposure compensation experimentation.*Digital Processing (technical)*It makes no sense to discuss this. Because of the agressive jpeg compression many post processing techniques will come out bad. It might help under the new rules to make your image smaller!!!!!! You are not limited to 640x480 I believe, but can also RESAMPLE (Lanczos / bibubic algoritm; try Irfanview if you don''t have an editor that can do that; DONT RESIZE, ALWAYS RESAMPLE!!!). That process might take some of the compression artefacts away and allow you to save at a higher compression level, close to 150kb. The small file might even allow for some sharpening without worsening the picture! Check the new rules about the file size and check the forums about resampling and saving.*My opinion*This is a very interesting picture (seriously, I don''t say this to make you feel better), but it is ruined by the camera. I hope that the new rules allow you to post something of better quality, because your approach to photography is promising.', '2002-12-03 14:52:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(161960, 8852, 3032, '<td valign="top">Try a 400x300 format for example.<br/>I tried it in Irfanfiew with this pic, it looked a lot better in that format. (resample using lanczos).<br/>It could also be saved at a much higher quality and the quality wasn''t lost in compression artefacts.<br/>It won''t work on all pictures, but it is something worth to experiment with.</td>', 'Try a 400x300 format for example.I tried it in Irfanfiew with this pic, it looked a lot better in that format. (resample using lanczos).It could also be saved at a much higher quality and the quality wasn''t lost in compression artefacts.It won''t work on all pictures, but it is something worth to experiment with.', '2002-12-03 15:00:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(161961, 8853, 4967, '<td valign="top">Wow... too bad you didn''t get one of the flags being raised by someone!</td>', 'Wow... too bad you didn''t get one of the flags being raised by someone!', '2002-11-25 01:37:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161962, 8853, 3540, '<td valign="top">The first thing I think when I see this picture is "underexposed."  I think it isn''t a totally bad thing to be a little dark here, just not to this degree.  I generally like his picture though.  The concept is very good.  The advantage to being dark is that the flags really stand out.  The disadvantage is that, well it looks very dreary, almost morbid and things are quite undefined.  Good luck - Inspzil</td>', 'The first thing I think when I see this picture is "underexposed."  I think it isn''t a totally bad thing to be a little dark here, just not to this degree.  I generally like his picture though.  The concept is very good.  The advantage to being dark is that the flags really stand out.  The disadvantage is that, well it looks very dreary, almost morbid and things are quite undefined.  Good luck - Inspzil', '2002-11-25 05:17:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161963, 8853, 1202, '<td valign="top">Composition: Subject Placement, Cropping, Background8,<br/>Technical: Focus, Exposure, Lighting, Processing5,<br/>Appeal: Is it Interesting, Motivating, Etc.? 6,<br/>Total Averaged Rating6.   Autool<br/>IMO the relationship between the title and picture are key elements in this challenge.  Too much of this nowdays.   I think you needed better light and more contrast.   How did it look in color, and did you try to save it by going to B/W?   If so this seldom works.<br/></td>', 'Composition: Subject Placement, Cropping, Background8,Technical: Focus, Exposure, Lighting, Processing5,Appeal: Is it Interesting, Motivating, Etc.? 6,Total Averaged Rating6.   AutoolIMO the relationship between the title and picture are key elements in this challenge.  Too much of this nowdays.   I think you needed better light and more contrast.   How did it look in color, and did you try to save it by going to B/W?   If so this seldom works.', '2002-11-25 10:30:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161964, 8853, 4482, '<td valign="top">sorry to say but in mourning the flags are at half-mast.. . good try though 3</td>', 'sorry to say but in mourning the flags are at half-mast.. . good try though 3', '2002-11-25 11:12:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161965, 8853, 714, '<td valign="top">This is great.  Good job.  It seems a bit dark.  Vote 7 Sonifo</td>', 'This is great.  Good job.  It seems a bit dark.  Vote 7 Sonifo', '2002-11-25 11:15:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161966, 8853, 4821, '<td valign="top">I wish this picture was lighter</td>', 'I wish this picture was lighter', '2002-11-25 12:33:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161967, 8853, 5120, '<td valign="top">This shot might benefit from a little more contrast or maybe just brightening it up more.  It looks kind of dark on my screen.<br/><br/>Greg<br/></td>', 'This shot might benefit from a little more contrast or maybe just brightening it up more.  It looks kind of dark on my screen.Greg', '2002-11-25 19:11:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161968, 8853, 2553, '<td valign="top">I think I would have liked this shot to be a little bit brighter, but overall I really like it a lot, and it carries a lot of emotion.  I do like the black and white.  lhall</td>', 'I think I would have liked this shot to be a little bit brighter, but overall I really like it a lot, and it carries a lot of emotion.  I do like the black and white.  lhall', '2002-11-25 19:40:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161969, 8853, 3859, '<td valign="top">Interesting shot, but it''s a little dark.</td>', 'Interesting shot, but it''s a little dark.', '2002-11-25 23:18:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161970, 8853, 4906, '<td valign="top">Picture is too dark, otherwise good.</td>', 'Picture is too dark, otherwise good.', '2002-11-26 10:14:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161971, 8853, 2792, '<td valign="top">Were you trying to go for gloomy?</td>', 'Were you trying to go for gloomy?', '2002-11-26 13:19:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161972, 8853, 4805, '<td valign="top">Oh this would have been so much nicer with a contrast enhancement...excellent composition but a bit too dark I think.</td>', 'Oh this would have been so much nicer with a contrast enhancement...excellent composition but a bit too dark I think.', '2002-11-26 15:35:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161973, 8853, 4648, '<td valign="top">You ruined the American flag with B&amp;W!  You lost 3 points for that.  Too dark.  I thought you lowered the flag for a fallen hero.  Better title needed.  Your picture doesn''t say your title.  And in my opinion in this challenge titles are important.  They say what you want your picture to lead us into read.  Not the best shot.  A little dark, maybe an over cast day.  Does make for a somber shot which is befitting the setting.  Since the memorial goes for raise flags I''ll have to accept them raised. PTL4  Looked it over and the photo deserves more than a 4, no matter my feelings about the flags - raised or half staff.  PTL6</td>', 'You ruined the American flag with B&W!  You lost 3 points for that.  Too dark.  I thought you lowered the flag for a fallen hero.  Better title needed.  Your picture doesn''t say your title.  And in my opinion in this challenge titles are important.  They say what you want your picture to lead us into read.  Not the best shot.  A little dark, maybe an over cast day.  Does make for a somber shot which is befitting the setting.  Since the memorial goes for raise flags I''ll have to accept them raised. PTL4  Looked it over and the photo deserves more than a 4, no matter my feelings about the flags - raised or half staff.  PTL6', '2002-11-26 20:05:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161974, 8853, 4514, '<td valign="top">Very Dramatic.  Good shot.</td>', 'Very Dramatic.  Good shot.', '2002-11-27 06:04:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161975, 8853, 5212, '<td valign="top">Very nice, good statement made with greyscale.  I gave it a 9</td>', 'Very nice, good statement made with greyscale.  I gave it a 9', '2002-11-28 02:01:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161976, 8853, 3018, '<td valign="top">It would''ve been better in color.</td>', 'It would''ve been better in color.', '2002-11-28 11:00:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161977, 8853, 3447, '<td valign="top">It''s a shame the weather was not more cooperative for your photo.   JEM</td>', 'It''s a shame the weather was not more cooperative for your photo.   JEM', '2002-11-28 13:53:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161978, 8853, 3532, '<td valign="top">Very gray and low contrast - probably underexposed.  Needs some real white highlights and some really dark darks.  I''m usually a fan of black and white, but with all the flags, I think this photo  might have benefited from color.</td>', 'Very gray and low contrast - probably underexposed.  Needs some real white highlights and some really dark darks.  I''m usually a fan of black and white, but with all the flags, I think this photo  might have benefited from color.', '2002-11-28 20:10:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161979, 8853, 4162, '<td valign="top">I think that colour would have been better here.  Its interesting in B/W but I think the colour would add interest.</td>', 'I think that colour would have been better here.  Its interesting in B/W but I think the colour would add interest.', '2002-11-28 22:18:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161980, 8853, 1280, '<td valign="top">On my monitor it appears too dark, but it sort of lends itself to the theme.  I like it.  Grayce</td>', 'On my monitor it appears too dark, but it sort of lends itself to the theme.  I like it.  Grayce', '2002-11-29 00:32:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161981, 8853, 2170, '<td valign="top">This is way too dark..  I think this would have been more effective in color as well.  muckpond.</td>', 'This is way too dark..  I think this would have been more effective in color as well.  muckpond.', '2002-11-30 17:23:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161982, 8853, 3247, '<td valign="top">Sullen. I like it.</td>', 'Sullen. I like it.', '2002-11-30 17:53:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161983, 8853, 5070, '<td valign="top">This would have been a good shot if lighter.</td>', 'This would have been a good shot if lighter.', '2002-11-30 21:30:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161984, 8853, 4186, '<td valign="top">wow. that''s so wonderfully gray. perfect use of color, really captures the mood. 10 sounds good to me.</td>', 'wow. that''s so wonderfully gray. perfect use of color, really captures the mood. 10 sounds good to me.', '2002-12-01 20:10:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161985, 8854, 4967, '<td valign="top">Yikes!  Hope you didn''t crash that truck just for this picture.  Good but could use a human aspect, a fireman, or a policeman, or a crying person or something.  Good try!</td>', 'Yikes!  Hope you didn''t crash that truck just for this picture.  Good but could use a human aspect, a fireman, or a policeman, or a crying person or something.  Good try!', '2002-11-25 01:27:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161986, 8854, 4493, '<td valign="top">Well done. Might have been useful to have the whole bed of the truck in the shot.</td>', 'Well done. Might have been useful to have the whole bed of the truck in the shot.', '2002-11-25 09:24:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161987, 8854, 4510, '<td valign="top">Great shot, incredible detail, the title says it all !!</td>', 'Great shot, incredible detail, the title says it all !!', '2002-11-25 10:54:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161988, 8854, 327, '<td valign="top">Okay.....right place at the right time. Nice job although I think the perspective could of been improved a bit. Still it''s clean, clear, good color, light. Justine</td>', 'Okay.....right place at the right time. Nice job although I think the perspective could of been improved a bit. Still it''s clean, clear, good color, light. Justine', '2002-11-25 14:13:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161989, 8854, 4514, '<td valign="top">Good shot bad title.  Crystal Clear.  Poor Ranger.  :-(</td>', 'Good shot bad title.  Crystal Clear.  Poor Ranger.  :-(', '2002-11-26 04:08:00.000000', NULL, 1);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(161990, 8854, 4906, '<td valign="top">Cropping is a bit tight at back end of truck.</td>', 'Cropping is a bit tight at back end of truck.', '2002-11-26 09:13:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161991, 8854, 3102, '<td valign="top">I hope you didn''t cause this accident :)  Nice job of capturing something that could have indeed landed in a newspaper -- excellent job of meeting the challenge!  I also like the slight reflection of the firetruck in the roof. -8  alansfreed</td>', 'I hope you didn''t cause this accident :)  Nice job of capturing something that could have indeed landed in a newspaper -- excellent job of meeting the challenge!  I also like the slight reflection of the firetruck in the roof. -8  alansfreed', '2002-11-26 13:04:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161992, 8854, 2983, '<td valign="top">I think having more of the environment around the truck would make it stand out more.</td>', 'I think having more of the environment around the truck would make it stand out more.', '2002-11-26 14:02:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161993, 8854, 3080, '<td valign="top">I looked for this shot all week.  Great capture. You got this at a good angle and  your framing/cropping are good as well.  focus is nice, and the lighting conditions were also good.  A great photo! ~Heather~</td>', 'I looked for this shot all week.  Great capture. You got this at a good angle and  your framing/cropping are good as well.  focus is nice, and the lighting conditions were also good.  A great photo! ~Heather~', '2002-11-26 14:50:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161994, 8854, 4411, '<td valign="top">No it doesn''t!<br/>A good photo, worthy of a newspaper.<br/>For an artier shot I would crop so that just the bonnet and windscreen were showing - but I don''t think that would fit the challenge as well.</td>', 'No it doesn''t!A good photo, worthy of a newspaper.For an artier shot I would crop so that just the bonnet and windscreen were showing - but I don''t think that would fit the challenge as well.', '2002-11-26 17:10:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161995, 8854, 4615, '<td valign="top">Or: Are you really safer in a SUV?</td>', 'Or: Are you really safer in a SUV?', '2002-11-26 18:42:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161996, 8854, 2170, '<td valign="top">I hope this wasn''t a setup shot!  LOL!  Way to be at the right plast at the right time.  The reflection of the fire engine in the roof of the truck is pretty powerful imagery as well, although it would probably be overlooked in a newspaper or magazine shot.  Great job!  muckpond</td>', 'I hope this wasn''t a setup shot!  LOL!  Way to be at the right plast at the right time.  The reflection of the fire engine in the roof of the truck is pretty powerful imagery as well, although it would probably be overlooked in a newspaper or magazine shot.  Great job!  muckpond', '2002-11-27 09:39:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161997, 8854, 3317, '<td valign="top">wow, you can see a fire truck reflected in the roof, cool. how did the authorities or participants in the accident feel about you taking pictures?</td>', 'wow, you can see a fire truck reflected in the roof, cool. how did the authorities or participants in the accident feel about you taking pictures?', '2002-11-27 21:52:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161998, 8854, 3273, '<td valign="top">Nice clear shot but it''s a little too tightly cropped for me.</td>', 'Nice clear shot but it''s a little too tightly cropped for me.', '2002-11-28 04:05:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(161999, 8854, 2279, '<td valign="top">Ouch that looks painful. Nice shot. 7. byetko.</td>', 'Ouch that looks painful. Nice shot. 7. byetko.', '2002-11-28 05:32:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(162000, 8854, 4648, '<td valign="top">Good cmposition with good execution.  Good subject, cropped a little tight.  Seems to need darking just a little maybe, the building in the background appear somewhat faded out.  Still a really good photo and title. PTL9</td>', 'Good cmposition with good execution.  Good subject, cropped a little tight.  Seems to need darking just a little maybe, the building in the background appear somewhat faded out.  Still a really good photo and title. PTL9', '2002-11-28 21:45:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(162001, 8854, 4776, '<td valign="top">Wow, real news. 8</td>', 'Wow, real news. 8', '2002-11-29 15:37:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(162002, 8854, 4305, '<td valign="top">of course it does! look there is proof!!!</td>', 'of course it does! look there is proof!!!', '2002-11-30 02:33:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(162003, 8854, 4596, '<td valign="top">Easy subject matter. Average effort.</td>', 'Easy subject matter. Average effort.', '2002-11-30 17:17:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(162004, 8854, 3247, '<td valign="top">Try this as B&amp;W. I think it will have more impact.</td>', 'Try this as B&W. I think it will have more impact.', '2002-11-30 18:21:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(162005, 8854, 2, '<td valign="top">Great job finding an exciting subject.  I''m not sure I like your choice of angle/framing, though.</td>', 'Great job finding an exciting subject.  I''m not sure I like your choice of angle/framing, though.', '2002-12-01 23:23:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(162006, 8854, 51167, '<td valign="top">Ok this is my first try at an in depth critique so don''t know anything too personal or if I miss something cause I''m learning and I figure I''ll learn things from helping out with the critique club.  This was one of my favorite shots of the week.<br/><br/>COMPOSITION - I like the angle where you took this shot.  At first I thought you were tilting the camera a little, but the houses in the background are straight.  It looks like the truck knocked the pole a little.  The exposure seems just a tad bright.  The reflections on the trucks roof are perfect for the situation.  I would have liked to see it cropped a little less on the right to get more of the truck''s back in the shot.  <br/><br/>BACKGROUND- The background seems fine for the situation.  It''s not cluttered with onlookers and you''ve blocked a lot of it with how close you are to the truck which is good, cause I don''t think it would have looked as good if the background had cars and was messy.  <br/><br/>CAMERA WORK- Focus and sharpness are good.  The DOF is good, I thought what it would have looked like with a bigger aperature, but then I thought that the background is fine.<br/><br/>Digital Processing- It is fine.  There are a few small artifacts or jaggies(whatever they are) around the grass in the shadow and the lines in the truck bed are a little jaggy.  But they are just small things.<br/><br/>My Opinion- As I said that this was one of my favorite shots.  It fit the theme perfectly, and it was very powerful.  The message of your title was great too.   Thanks for sharing this shot was great!</td>', 'Ok this is my first try at an in depth critique so don''t know anything too personal or if I miss something cause I''m learning and I figure I''ll learn things from helping out with the critique club.  This was one of my favorite shots of the week.COMPOSITION - I like the angle where you took this shot.  At first I thought you were tilting the camera a little, but the houses in the background are straight.  It looks like the truck knocked the pole a little.  The exposure seems just a tad bright.  The reflections on the trucks roof are perfect for the situation.  I would have liked to see it cropped a little less on the right to get more of the truck''s back in the shot.  BACKGROUND- The background seems fine for the situation.  It''s not cluttered with onlookers and you''ve blocked a lot of it with how close you are to the truck which is good, cause I don''t think it would have looked as good if the background had cars and was messy.  CAMERA WORK- Focus and sharpness are good.  The DOF is good, I thought what it would have looked like with a bigger aperature, but then I thought that the background is fine.Digital Processing- It is fine.  There are a few small artifacts or jaggies(whatever they are) around the grass in the shadow and the lines in the truck bed are a little jaggy.  But they are just small things.My Opinion- As I said that this was one of my favorite shots.  It fit the theme perfectly, and it was very powerful.  The message of your title was great too.   Thanks for sharing this shot was great!', '2002-12-03 02:25:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(162007, 8855, 3280, '<td valign="top">Very nice shot, it is unfortunate that the other goose is there with his head cut off though.  It really distracts from the front goose.  DPz</td>', 'Very nice shot, it is unfortunate that the other goose is there with his head cut off though.  It really distracts from the front goose.  DPz', '2002-11-25 00:47:00.000000', NULL, 1),
