(167145, 8673, 255, '<td valign="top">i really love pictures of old churches! i took a million myself in italy! ;) this one has a sort of haunted feel to it, perhaps because of the way the gravestones are leaning---but i love that about it! i also really like the shadows--they could almost be darker in my opinion. the composition is nice, and although i find myself wondering if it would have looked like if you had taken a couple of steps to the left, im glad you didnt because you would have lost the shadows from the gravestones. the upward angle is really cool, it adds to the spooky feel by seeming like the church is really looming over you. technically, the focus seems just a tiny bit soft and the color almost monotone--like i said before, i might have liked to see a bigger difference in the stones and shadows, but that is just me! all in all, really nice photo! keep up the good work!</td>', 'i really love pictures of old churches! i took a million myself in italy! ;) this one has a sort of haunted feel to it, perhaps because of the way the gravestones are leaning---but i love that about it! i also really like the shadows--they could almost be darker in my opinion. the composition is nice, and although i find myself wondering if it would have looked like if you had taken a couple of steps to the left, im glad you didnt because you would have lost the shadows from the gravestones. the upward angle is really cool, it adds to the spooky feel by seeming like the church is really looming over you. technically, the focus seems just a tiny bit soft and the color almost monotone--like i said before, i might have liked to see a bigger difference in the stones and shadows, but that is just me! all in all, really nice photo! keep up the good work!', '2002-12-09 03:39:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(167413, 8689, 4628, '<td valign="top">Very well done...  The photoshop effect turned out great. The only real problem in my opinion is the red of the tail light of the passing car (Though i realize theres nothing you could have done about that by dpchallenge rules)</td>', 'Very well done...  The photoshop effect turned out great. The only real problem in my opinion is the red of the tail light of the passing car (Though i realize theres nothing you could have done about that by dpchallenge rules)', '2002-12-09 09:42:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(177220, 8697, 1005, '<td valign="top">Once again, the Critique Club strikes first and best.  This shot was a little too title dependant, even for me.  Still, I gave it a 7.  I thought there were quite a few good aspects and very few bad ones.  Without the title, I think my interest level for this would have been less.</td>', 'Once again, the Critique Club strikes first and best.  This shot was a little too title dependant, even for me.  Still, I gave it a 7.  I thought there were quite a few good aspects and very few bad ones.  Without the title, I think my interest level for this would have been less.', '2002-12-23 18:01:06.000000', NULL, 0);
<br/> <br/>The best time for shooting this is on a cold clear Sunday morning, from the ice in the harbour when it is there and stand back more. Because you are deeper in comparison to the walls, the angle of view takes out the cars and most modern stuff and shows the tower in its ''natural'' surroundings with old houses in the background. Doesn''t happen often.<br/> <br/>So now it was centered. That''s why I stood back and let the wooden landing stage lead the eye into the pic.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-01-14 13:14:42.</i></td>', 'About the right and left side: This is the cleanest crop possible. More to the right is a sign for tourists and a modern kind of fish boot and parkinglots in front of the houses. More to the left is a pump for ships and there were some high cars spoiling the classic buildings. The best time for shooting this is on a cold clear Sunday morning, from the ice in the harbour when it is there and stand back more. Because you are deeper in comparison to the walls, the angle of view takes out the cars and most modern stuff and shows the tower in its ''natural'' surroundings with old houses in the background. Doesn''t happen often. So now it was centered. That''s why I stood back and let the wooden landing stage lead the eye into the pic.', '2003-01-14 13:13:04.000000', '2003-01-14 13:14:42.000000', 0),
